text:
sophia: quick question — i'm moving vectorizer-prod to use the central kms key in billing account. terraform draft attached. wondering about the cleanest way to grant IRSA pods decrypt without opening the key policy to the whole account.

sophia: current idea: create a cross-account IAM role in billing account that trusts the OIDC provider + the namespace/serviceaccount, then add that role as a principal in the key policy. downside: extra role to maintain. thoughts? :thinking_face:

tim: that sounds reasonable. alternative is to add a condition on the key policy allowing sts:AssumeRole with aws:SourceIdentity/session tags, but iirc kms key policies don't see session tags.

harpreet: fyi we hit a weird ordering issue last week where provider alias + tf resource ordering caused the key policy apply to race with role creation. you might need an explicit depends_on on the role when applying the key policy resource.

sophia: ok good to know. here's the sketch of the terraform bits — can someone sanity-check?
```hcl
# in billing acct repo
resource "aws_iam_role" "irsa_vectorizer" {
  name = "irsa-vectorizer-crossrole"
  assume_role_policy = data.aws_iam_policy_document.irsa_assume.json
}

data "aws_iam_policy_document" "irsa_assume" {
  statement {
    actions = ["sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity"]
    principals { type = "Federated"; identifiers = [var.oidc_provider_arn] }
    condition { test = "StringEquals"; variable = "${var.oidc_provider_url}:sub"; values = ["system:serviceaccount:ml-prod:vectorizer"] }
  }
}

# key policy snippet
resource "aws_kms_key" "central" {
  policy = data.aws_iam_policy_document.kms_key.json
}

data "aws_iam_policy_document" "kms_key" {
  statement {
    sid = "AllowCrossAccountRole"
    principals { type = "AWS"; identifiers = [aws_iam_role.irsa_vectorizer.arn] }
    actions = ["kms:Decrypt", "kms:GenerateDataKey*"]
    resources = ["*"]
  }
}
```

sophia: is the principal ARN in the key policy the right way? or should we be using a kms:ViaService or conditions on aws:PrincipalTag?

tim: principal ARN is fine. if you want tighter scope, you can add a Condition like "StringEquals": {"aws:PrincipalTag/k8s-sa": "ml-prod:vectorizer"} but then you must ensure the role gets that tag and session tags propagate — which depends on how pods assume the role.

harpreet: session tag propagation is the annoying bit. IRSA uses STS:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity and source identity is set by the token controller. in our experience, tags assigned to the role (aws:TagKeys on assume role) don't automatically become session tags unless you use OpenID Connect session tags mapping. Might be simpler to rely on the role ARN as the principal in the key policy.

oliver: small nit: when you create the role in a different repo (billing acct) and reference it from infra repo (central key), you'll need to import the role or output the arn and feed it into the key repo. otherwise TF tries to create both and ordering gets messy. we solved this with a one-way data source + a manual apply step on role creation first.

sophia: got it. so plan: create cross-account role in billing, tag it with owner/team, then add that role ARN into key policy in central account. i'll add depends_on on the role data if possible and document manual apply step.

tim: also add a kms grant for the role instead of only key policy? grants are useful for short-lived operations and fine-grained operations e.g., re-encrypt. but remember grants expire on key rotation unless re-created.

infra-bot: deploy check: terraform plan in central-key repo returned 2 resources to add, 0 to change. No drift detected. :white_check_mark:

harpreet: thanks — last thing: watch for kms:Encrypt vs kms:GenerateDataKey* on the worker path. if vectorizer does local envelope encryption, it needs GenerateDataKeyWithoutPlaintext or GenerateDataKey depending on flow. double-check code.

sophia: noted. i'll update the PR with the role creation plan and a short runbook for the 2-step apply. ping me if you want to pair on the apply tomorrow morning. :pray:

oliver: happy to pair, 10am PT works for me.

sophia: thanks team, will follow up with PR link shortly.
